<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Homebrew on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/homebrew/</link><description>Recent content in Homebrew on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 12:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/homebrew/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Fuzebox, open source gaming</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/fuzebox-open-source-gaming/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Nov 2008 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/fuzebox-open-source-gaming/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 18 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Take me back to my 8bit gaming youth? &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://hackaday.com/2008/11/25/fuzebox-open-source-gaming/"&gt;Fuzebox, open source gaming&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="snap_preview"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-6283" title="fuzebox" src="http://hackadaycom.files.wordpress.com/2008/11/fuzebox.jpg?w=450&amp;amp;h=289" alt="fuzebox" height="289" width="450" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adafruit has just put their &lt;a rel="nofollow" title="Uzebox - The ATMega Game Console" target="_blank" href="http://belogic.com/uzebox/"&gt;Uzebox&lt;/a&gt; based console into production. The &lt;a rel="nofollow" title="Adafruit Industries, Unique &amp;amp; fun DIY electronics and kits" target="_blank" href="http://www.adafruit.com/index.php?main_page=index&amp;amp;cPath=30"&gt;Fuzebox&lt;/a&gt; is an 8bit game console based around the ATmega644-20PU microcontroller. Full 256 color 240×224 resolution video output is provide by either a composite connection or svideo. There is an SD card slot on board for future expansion. The chip takes care of all the I/O, so you just need to write your game code in C on top of it.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Nintendo DS Homebrew</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nintendo-ds-homebrew/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Nov 2008 10:39:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nintendo-ds-homebrew/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a onblur="try {parent.deselectBloggerImageGracefully();} catch(e) {}" href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh5xqG0v9vbKwtJsUqPN6a8uqPgjKzcp5Hqr5IXkh21FZ7dN7q7R8ewZYQiTYVLwSjeq14Y8H8qooWh0GlPHiedIpdR-OnUY7P1o220ryWUA3Kj_OZF2WNiAPnJvsSr1VT4IFX3GueSIEw/s1600-h/Nintendo_DS_Lite_Black_Console.jpg"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0pt 10px 10px 0pt; float: left; cursor: pointer; width: 200px; height: 200px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh5xqG0v9vbKwtJsUqPN6a8uqPgjKzcp5Hqr5IXkh21FZ7dN7q7R8ewZYQiTYVLwSjeq14Y8H8qooWh0GlPHiedIpdR-OnUY7P1o220ryWUA3Kj_OZF2WNiAPnJvsSr1VT4IFX3GueSIEw/s200/Nintendo_DS_Lite_Black_Console.jpg" alt="" id="BLOGGER_PHOTO_ID_5268090940044084994" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been getting extremely excited about the Nintendo DS home brew scene. The &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/5t86zh"&gt;Spectrum&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/5jbpbc"&gt;SNES&lt;/a&gt; emulators look like a win, also there is a &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/6n6q3j"&gt;Doom&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://quake.drunkencoders.com/"&gt;Quake&lt;/a&gt; port available. Happy days&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip;..&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>